#
# Dev environment overrides for scripts/dev.sh. Copy to scripts/dev.env
# (gitignored) and uncomment what you want to change.
#
# All defaults below are deliberately shifted by +10000 from the UAT
# defaults so dev can run alongside a UAT/another service stack on the same
# machine without port collisions. The api default is 3030 specifically
# because port 3000 is owned by another service on the host —
# NEVER use 3000 for dev API or you'll fight over the socket.

# ─── Host port mappings (shifted from UAT defaults) ─────────────────────
# POSTGRES_PORT_DEV=15432
# VALKEY_PORT_DEV=16379

# ─── OSRM (SHARED with UAT — no second container) ───────────────────────
# Running a second OSRM instance OOMs the host (NL-foot extract peaks at
# ~5-6 GiB during preprocessing). Dev points at UAT's already-running
# osrm via host-published port 5000. Read-only HTTP calls — no risk to
# UAT. Override if your UAT runs OSRM on a non-default port.
# OSRM_URL_DEV=http://localhost:5000

# ─── Landuse (ADR-0009) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev reads landuse_polygons directly from the dev Postgres (just like
# UAT does from the UAT Postgres). Run the one-shot import once via the
# UAT compose file (or against the dev DB directly) to populate it.
# No env var needed in dev.env — there's no separate landuse service.

# ─── Local processes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API_PORT_DEV=3030       # DO NOT set to 3000 (another service on the host)
# WEB_PORT_DEV=5173       # Vite default; safe to keep

# ─── Raw GPX uploads (preserved for /admin/uploads/:id/reprocess) ──────
# Default: $ROOT/data/uploads (gitignored). Override to share a folder
# across multiple checkouts or to push to an external disk.
# UPLOADS_DIR_DEV=/var/lib/gctp/uploads

# ─── Dev DB ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Distinct db name (gctp_dev, not gctp) so a `psql` connection string
# makes the dev-vs-uat distinction visible at a glance.
# POSTGRES_USER_DEV=gctp
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD_DEV=gctp-dev
# POSTGRES_DB_DEV=gctp_dev

# ─── Planner ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TOUR_PLANNER=greedy
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# ─── Auth (M6, ADR-0021) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev defaults to the bypass so `pnpm dev` and Playwright e2e attribute every
# request to dev@gctp.local with no login round-trip (FR-P10). The bypass is
# hard-refused under NODE_ENV=production. Comment this out to exercise the real
# login flow locally.
AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=1
# Only needed if you turn the bypass off and exercise Google OAuth locally.
# AUTH_SESSION_SECRET=dev-insecure-session-secret
# Where to land after a successful sign-in (defaults to "/").
# OAUTH_POST_LOGIN_REDIRECT=/
# Google OAuth (authorization-code flow). Set all three to enable the
# /auth/google routes locally; leave unset and they return 503. Create a Web
# OAuth client in Google Cloud Console with the redirect URI below as an
# authorized URI, and add your account as a Test user while the consent screen
# is in Testing. Use a dev-only client — keep the real secrets OUT of the repo
# (this is the gitignored dev.env, never dev.env.example). The dev redirect goes
# through the Vite proxy on :5173, which forwards /api to the api on :3030.
# OAUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# OAUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# OAUTH_GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/api/auth/google/callback
# Registration captcha (FR-P5, Gate 1.4). Set BOTH to exercise Turnstile on
# /register locally (also turn the bypass off above so the register flow runs).
# Cloudflare's "always passes" TESTING keys work on localhost with no account
# and need no real domain — siteverify still runs (needs outbound internet):
#   VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
# Leave both unset to keep open registration in dev (the default).
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET=
